TASK Replace the placeholder README with a concise accurate one — 2026-10-22 12:51:46
GOAL Give README.md a short, accurate explanation of Promptbook for people who find the `ptbk` package on npm or the repository on GitHub, in place of the current `TODO` placeholder.
The owner removed the previous 95-line README on 2026-10-21 (commit a93659cbbf, "Cleanup awful README") and left only `TODO`, without recording what the replacement should look like. The removed version was a dense list of nearly every command, flag and configuration setting. The owner's initial brief assigns README upkeep to Community, but the shape of the replacement is the owner's decision: first ask the owner with `ask_user` about the intended audience, approximate length and essential sections. Offer a concrete short default (for example purpose, requirements, installation, a first-project quick start and links into specs/) and also the choice to keep the placeholder because the owner will write the README personally. Follow the answer; if the owner keeps the placeholder, change nothing.
The package checks only require README.md to exist, so `TODO` passes them, and the file is part of the published npm package: version 0.119.0-26 on npm still carries the old text, while the tagged but unpublished 0.119.0-30 and any later release would publish the placeholder.
When writing, verify every command, option and example against the current implementation (`node bin/ptbk.js help` and the relevant `help <command>`), describe only shipped behavior and link to specs/ for detailed rules instead of copying them. Do not restore the removed text wholesale. Use no promotional claims, quotes or promises, and keep links to other repository files valid. Record the change in changelog/_current-preversion.md. Do not publish to npm or post anything externally.
